            <ArticleTitle>The effect of endotoxin on nociception in mice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>115-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The possible antinociceptive activity of endotoxin was studied in mice. The antinociceptive properties of endotoxin (0.0003, 0.003, 0.03, 0.3 and 3 mg/kg, i.p.) were evaluated using the phenylbenzoquinone-induced writhing test. The antinociceptive activity of endotoxin was more potent than that of aminopyrine and morphine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
